      "problem": "${(2{x}^{-2}y)}^{-3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the power of product rule and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}^{-2}y)^{-3} & = \\\\ {2}^{-3}{({x}^{-2})}^{-3}{({y}^{1})}^{-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}\\cdot {x}^{(-2)(-3)}\\cdot {y}^{(1)(-3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}\\cdot {x}^{6}\\cdot {y}^{-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{6}{y}^{-3}}{8} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
